Alembic migrations live here. See `replit.md` -> "Schema Migrations
(Alembic — April 2026)" for the full contract.

TL;DR
-----
Existing 80+ tables are still created by `init_db()` in `app.py` on
first boot (idempotent CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS). That code path is
frozen — do NOT add new columns or tables to it.

To add a new column or table going forward:

    alembic revision -m "add foo column to bar"

Edit the new file in `migrations/versions/`. On the next app boot
`alembic upgrade head` runs automatically and applies the change.
